      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-100163",
      ":question/problem": "Find the exact solution of the equation ${7}^{x+4}=5.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we take ${log}_{7}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{7}^{x+4} & =5 \\\\ {log}_{7}⁡({7}^{x+4}) & ={log}_{7}⁡(5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that ${log}_{b}⁡({b}^{c})=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx+4={log}_{7}⁡(5)\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+4 & ={log}_{7}⁡(5) \\\\ x & ={log}_{7}⁡(5)-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x={log}_{7}⁡(5)-4.$"
    },
